; specs/course/ternary-computing.t27 -- the t27 course "The ternary machine"
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/course.t27: the constant schema, every test block below, every
; widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle named
; by specs/course/ternary-computing-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/ternary-computing) and a byte-identical copy of this file at
; public/learn/ternary-computing.t27. ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 8 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3: why
; three, balanced ternary, Kleene logic, adders, multiplying without a multiplier, trits in binary
; memory, the TRI-27 instruction word, a ternary machine, three-way answers and ternary neurons.
; Every lesson opens one live widget and one spec. The 27 widgets (tc-*) draw through
; public/widgets/ternary-kit.js and compute nothing: every number is a call into a compiled t27
; spec, gHashTag/t27 specs/ternary/trits.t27 and radix_economy.t27 (t27#8979) or
; specs/isa/ternary_encoding.t27, held to its source by scripts/widget-logic.mjs.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no number of its own. Every number in a lesson comes from
; the spec it opens or the widget it shows, and each of those names its own source. Where a lesson
; spec is a different machine from the widget -- ternary_full_adder.t27 and ternary_ripple_adder.t27
; are binary adders built from ternary neurons -- the lesson text says so.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module ternary_computing;

